cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "icarus: data-driven heat flux prediction from infrared thermography"
authors:
  - family-names: Twum-Barima
    given-names: Raymond
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-06-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/twumbarimaraymond1-coder/icarus"
keywords:
  - heat transfer
  - infrared thermography
  - proper orthogonal decomposition
  - dynamic mode decomposition
  - machine learning
  - flow boiling
abstract: >-
  icarus provides a full pipeline from raw infrared camera data to trained
  heat-flux prediction models using Proper Orthogonal Decomposition (POD),
  Dynamic Mode Decomposition (DMD), and neural networks, including a
  multi-dataset registry for cross-dataset (leave-one-surface-out)
  generalisation evaluation.
